{:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191813} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191814} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191815} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191816}] :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191811}] :question/math-academy-id "q-343711" :question/problem "$U = \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}, V = \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the matrices $U$ and $V$ above. Let $X$ be a $2 \\cdot 3$ standardized observation matrix, where each row represents one observation and each column represents one feature. Given that $X = UΣV^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $X$, what is the second principal component of the data?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193315 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u_{3}u^{T}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191818} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u_{3}v_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191819} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191820} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218